<title>ITALY: CIR wants lower Olivetti stake.</title>
<headline>CIR wants lower Olivetti stake.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian industrial holding company CIR, owned by financier Carlo De Benedetti, said it wants to lower its stake in information technology group Olivetti to around five percent.</p>
<p>CIR Managing Director Rodolfo De Benedetti told a shareholders' meeting that the group's aim was to bring the shareholding down from its current level.</p>
<p>CIR told the stock exchange watchdog authority Consob on April 9 that its stake stood at 6.29 percent, down from 12.8 percent at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>--Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
